Subject: Write the GTK 4 colours and Breeze decorations from the first login

At the first login of a new user ~/.config/gtk-4.0 does not exist when the
module writes gtk.css and colors.css, and QFile does not create a missing
directory, so a GTK 4 or libadwaita program wears stock Adwaita until the
next colour change. Create each GTK config directory before writing into
it.

At the same login kconf_update writes gtk-theme-name=Breeze into
settings.ini while kded is already running, after the module has read the
file, so the module takes the theme for unset, removes Breeze's
window_decorations.css and writes no decoration assets. When settings.ini
names no theme, take the name from GSettings, which holds the same one.

diff --git a/kded/config_editor/custom_css.cpp b/kded/config_editor/custom_css.cpp
